# win32u: Do not discard dmPosition in add_modes
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/11497 state=opened
# When modes_count == 1, physical is set to \*modes, but this is actually not equivalent to just setting to \*current (which theoretically should be the same mode) since \*current also carries information about positioning. Strictly speaking, positioning information shouldn't be part of the supported modes.

I think under all circumstances setting the physical mode to the current mode is the desired behaviour, and ensures that win32 is aware of the actual virtual monitor size.

Without this change, (at least for Wayland) NtUserGetSystemMetrics(SM_CXVIRTUALSCREEN) will only return the width of the largest attached screen (same for `Y`).
--- dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -2217,7 +2217,7 @@ static void add_modes( const DEVMODEW *current, UINT host_modes_count, const DEV
         modes_count = 1;
     }
 
-    physical = modes_count == 1 ? *modes : *current;
+    if (current) physical = *current;
     if (ctx->is_primary) ctx->primary = *current;
 
     detached.dmPelsWidth = 0;

